"Digital Object Identiﬁer (DOI) https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-023-04764-z (https://refubium.fu-berlin.de/bitstream/handle/fub188/39952/s00220-023-04764-z.pdf?isAllowed=y&save=y&sequence=2)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form ... Abstract: We prove the positivity of Lyapunov exponents for the normal form of a Hopf\nDigital Object Identiﬁer (DOI) https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-023-04764-z\nCommun. Math. Phys. 402, 1807–1843 (2023)\nCommunications in\nMathematical\nPhysics\nPositive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form\nwith Additive Noise\nDennis Chemnitz\n, Maximilian Engel\nInstitut für Mathematik, Freie Universität Berlin, Arnimallee 6, 14195 Berlin, Germany.\nE-mail: dennis.chemnitz2@fu-berlin.de; maximilian.engel@fu-berlin.de\nReceived: 13 December 2022 / Accepted: 10 May 2023\nPublished online: 26 June 2023 – © The Author(s) 2023\nAbstract: We prove the positivity of Lyapunov exponents for the normal form of a Hopf\nbifurcation, perturbed by additive white noise, under sufﬁciently strong shear strength.\nThis completes a series of related results for simpliﬁed situations which we can exploit\nby studying suitable limits of the shear and noise parameters. The crucial technical\ningredient for making this approach rigorous is a result on the continuity of Lyapunov\nexponents via Furstenberg–Khasminskii formulas.\n1. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGeneralizations of Carmichael numbers I (https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.1867)\nciteturn2academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.5 years ago; Title: Generalizations of Carmichael numbers I\nAuthors: Romeo Meštrović ... A composite positive integer $n$ is said to be a {\\it weak Carmichael number} if $$ \\sum_{\\gcd(k,n)=1\\atop 1\\le k\\le n-1}k^{n-1}\\equiv \\varphi(n) \\pmod{n}. \\leqno(1) $$ It is proved that a composite positive integer $n$ is a weak Carmichael number if and only if $p-1\\mid n-1$ for every prime divisor $p$ of $n$.\nTitle: Generalizations of Carmichael numbers I\nAuthors: Romeo Meštrović\nDate: Sat May  4 01:36:32 2013\n\nA composite positive integer $n$ is said to be a {\\it weak Carmichael number} if $$ \\sum_{\\gcd(k,n)=1\\atop 1\\le k\\le n-1}k^{n-1}\\equiv \\varphi(n) \\pmod{n}. \\leqno(1) $$ It is proved that a composite positive integer $n$ is a weak Carmichael number if and only if $p-1\\mid n-1$ for every prime divisor $p$ of $n$. This together with Korselt's criterion yields the fact that every Carmichael number is also a weak Carmichael number. In this paper we mainly investigate arithmetic properties of weak Carmichael numbers. Motivated by the investigations of Carmichael numbers in the last hundred years, here we establish several related results, notions, examples and computatinoal searches for weak Carmichael numbers and numbers closely related to weak Carmichael numbers. Furthermore, using the software {\\tt Mathematica 8}, we present the table containing all non-prime powers weak Carmichael numbers less than $2\\times 10^6$. Motivated by heuristic arguments, our computations and some old conjectures and results for Carmichael numbers, we propose several conjectures for weak Carmichael numbers and for some other classes of Carmichael like numbers. Finally, we consider weak Carmichael numbers in light of Fermat primality test. We believe that it can be of interest to involve certain particular classes of weak Carmichael numbers in some problems concerning Fermat-like primality tests and the generalized Riemann hypothesis.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPositive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise (https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.06547)\nciteturn2academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.9 years ago; Title: Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise\nTitle: Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise\nAuthors: Dennis Chemnitz, Maximilian Engel\nDate: Tue Dec 13 12:59:33 2022\n\nWe prove the positivity of Lyapunov exponents for the normal form of a Hopf bifurcation, perturbed by additive white noise, under sufficiently strong shear strength. This completes a series of related results for simplified situations which we can exploit by studying suitable limits of the shear and noise parameters. The crucial technical ingredient for making this approach rigorous is a result on the continuity of Lyapunov exponents via Furstenberg Khasminskii formulas.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRefubium - Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise (https://refubium.fu-berlin.de/handle/fub188/39952?show=full)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; # Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise\n# Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise\n\ndc.​contributor.​author\n\nChemnitz, Dennis\n\ndc.​contributor.​author\n\nEngel, Maximilian\n\ndc.​date.​accessioned\n\n2023-08-28T07:42:15Z\n\ndc.​date.​available\n\n2023-08-28T07:42:15Z\n\ndc.​date.​issued\n\n2023\n\ndc.​identifier.​uri\n\nhttps://refubium.fu-berlin.de/handle/fub188/39952\n\ndc.​identifier.​uri\n\nhttp://dx.doi.org/10.17169/refubium-39674\n\ndc.​description.​abstract\n\nWe prove the positivity of Lyapunov exponents for the normal form of a Hopf bifurcation, perturbed by additive white noise, under sufficiently strong shear strength. This completes a series of related results for simplified situations which we can exploit by studying suitable limits of the shear and noise parameters. The crucial technical ingredient for making this approach rigorous is a result on the continuity of Lyapunov exponents via Furstenberg–Khasminskii formulas.\n\ndc.​format.​extent\n\n37 Seiten\n\ndc.​language\n\neng\n\ndc.​subject\n\nPositive Lyapunov Exponent\n\nen\n\ndc.​subject\n\nHopf Nor